          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Cunninghamia konishii, also known as Taiwanese China fir, is an endangered species of tree in the cypress family, Cupressaceae. It is native to southeast China (Fujian), Taiwan, Laos and Vietnam."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Taxonomy\nAlthough C. konishii is treated as a distinct species by many sources, it has also been suggested that it is conspecific with C. lanceolata."
          }
        ]
